==English==

===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:der|fr:inactif|tree=1}}
From {{der|en|fr|inactif}}. {{piecewise doublet|en|unactive}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈæktɪv/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-inactive.wav|a=UK}}
* {{rhymes|en|æktɪv|s=3}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Not [[active]], [[temporarily]] or [[permanently]].
#: {{ux|en|The volcano is '''inactive''', but is only dormant.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Inactive''' user accounts may be deleted after 90 days.}}
# Not engaging in physical activity.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2021|author=Suzanne Byrd|title=Practical Tips on Supporting Boys with ADHD|text={{...}} exercise in general will lead to dramatic improvements in comparison with an '''inactive''' lifestyle.}}
# Not [[functioning]] or [[operating]]; [[broken down]]
#: {{ux|en|The photocopier is '''inactive''' pending repair.}}
# [[retired|Retired]] from [[duty]] or [[service]].
#: {{ux|en|Admiral Jones is now on the '''inactive''' list.}}
# {{lb|en|chemistry}} [[relatively|Relatively]] [[inert]].
#: {{ux|en|Aluminium is '''inactive''' towards water.}}
# {{lb|en|physics}} Showing no [[optical]] [[activity]] in [[polarized]] [[light]].
#: {{ux|en|Synthetic glycine is optically '''inactive''' as it contains equal amounts of the d- and l- form.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|not active}} {{l|en|dull}}, {{l|en|dormant}}; see also [[Thesaurus:inactive]]
* {{sense|not functioning or operating}} {{l|en|idle}}

====Antonyms====
* {{antsense|not active}} {{l|en|active}}

